  "reason": "Evidence: The two largest gains in the search came from (1) switching to multiprofile (0.535→0.629) and (2) switching RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (0.635→0.706). The current best (config_037: scvi_n200, vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) sits at 0.706 acc. The RNA encoder is the dimension with the largest observed effect size, and we have not yet tested scgpt, a learned generative encoder that could capture richer single-cell structure than scvi_n200. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder in the otherwise-optimized multimodal multiprofile setting? config_049 (scgpt, vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable swap against config_037, isolating the encoder effect. Why best use of budget: If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, we identify a new best direction; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 is the right encoder and can redirect exploration toward aggregation/fusion refinements. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty on the highest-impact design axis, making this the most informative next step under a limited budget."
